5 - Files
    -----

    A001_00_Premises.v

      Stdlib re-export hub and minimal contract layer. Defines the abstract
      encoder/decoder types, the roundtrip and injectivity specifications, and
      the package contract.

    A001_02__Base_Fibonacci.v

      Fibonacci arithmetic and the carryless shape. Defines `fib`, `sum_fib`,
      the greedy support extractor `Z0`, the cutoff search `r0`, and a
      parametric `pair` / `unpair` taking a support engine as input. Establishes
      the Fibonacci recurrence and cutoff lemmas.

    A001_03__Zeckendorf_Correctness.v

      Correctness of the greedy extractor: `Z0` produces a valid support summing
      to its input (`Z0_sound`, `Z0_valid`), and valid supports are canonical
      (`Z0_of_sum_fib`, `Zeckendorf_unique`).

    A001_04__Carryless_Bands.v

      The even and odd Fibonacci-index embeddings are gap-2 separated, so their
      union is itself a valid Zeckendorf support and is recovered from the code
      by parity (`Z0_pair_is_concat`, `Z0_even_split`, `Z0_odd_split`).

    A001_05__Pair_Unpair_Correct.v

      Defines `encode` and `decode` as the carryless construction over `Z0` and
      `r0`, and proves the headline theorems `decode_encode` and
      `encode_injective`. Derives `decode_encode_fst`, `decode_encode_snd`,
      `support_of_encode`, and worked instances at (1,1) and (3,5).

    A001_94_IO.v

      Extraction-facing IO dispatcher. Defines `IO_Query`, `IO_Result`,
      `Code_Status`, and the endpoints `Paired_AB`, `Unpaired_C`,
      `Check_Pairing`, `In_Imageb`, `Status_Of_Code`, and `A001_IO`. Provides a
      compact `*_Z` view, so `vm_compute` need not print large Peano numerals.

    A001_95_API.v

      Stable package API. Re-exports the certified theorem surface.

    A001_97_Artifacts.v

      Redirects `Print Assumptions` for the two headline theorems into
      `_appendix/_assumptions/` and extracts `A001_Encode_Decode` and
      `A001_Carryless_Pairing_IO`. Both reports are closed.

    _appendix/_artifacts/

      Extracted OCaml: `A001_Encode_Decode.{ml,mli}` and
      `A001_Carryless_Pairing_IO.{ml,mli}`.

    _appendix/_assumptions/

      Redirected `Print Assumptions` output for `decode_encode` and
      `encode_injective`.

    _appendix/python_companion/

      Auxiliary Python workspace for empirical probes against the extracted
      OCaml surface. Not part of the certified development.


6 - API
    ---

    The public theorem surface is exposed by

      `From A001 Require Import A001_95_API.`

    Public surface by use case:

    Minimal contract vocabulary:

      encode_t                : Type                                        (00)
      decode_t                : Type                                        (00)
      decode_encode_spec      : encode_t -> decode_t -> Prop                (00)
      encode_injective_spec   : encode_t -> Prop                            (00)
      pairing_contract        : encode_t -> decode_t -> Prop                (00)

    Certified `nat` surface:

      encode           : nat -> nat -> nat                                  (05)
      decode           : nat -> nat * nat                                   (05)

    Dispatcher and inspection:

      IO_Query, IO_Result, Code_Status                                      (94)
      A001_IO          : IO_Query -> IO_Result                              (94)
      A001_IO_Z        : IO_Query -> IO_Result_Z                            (94)
      Check_Pairing    : nat -> nat                                         (94)
      In_Imageb        : nat -> bool                                        (94)
      Status_Of_Code   : nat -> Code_Status                                 (94)

    Certified theorems:

      decode_encode : forall a b,
        decode (encode a b) = (a, b)

      encode_injective : forall a b a' b',
        encode a b = encode a' b' -> a = a' /\ b = b'


7 - Notes
    -----

    The `*_Z` views render compact decimal integers, which is convenient for
    interactive examples:

    Eval vm_compute in (A001_IO_Z (Pair_Query 12 33)).
    Eval vm_compute in (A001_IO_Z (Inspect_Query (Paired_AB 12 33))).
    Eval vm_compute in (Compute_Pair_Unpair_Check_Z 12 33).
